      "side": 1,
      "message": "You don\u0027t need this lock, the phony singleton is not parallel so it doesn\u0027t run concurrent with any other singletons, and all singletons run after all modules.  Line 68 is loading the same phony map and accessing it without a lock, and if it did need a lock it would imply a logic race condition where it could write out the list of phonies and then something else could add to the list after it has already been written.",
